/-! # BlowupB.Uniform — aggregate = physical on complete blowups, for every family

**Theorem** (`physDiv_of_isIntDiv_uniform`). Let `F` be any family of partitioned triangle types
(multisets of size `3`), and `G` the complete `F`-blowup of a partition `p` with at least `5`
vertices in every class. Then every integrally `F`-divisible edge set of `G` (Definition 13.5)
lies in the physical lattice generated by the `F`-copies of `G`.

No finite per-family hypothesis is needed (compare `RepComplete` in `RepHost`). The threshold
`5` matches the computational gate: with `≤ 4` vertices per class the statement fails for
families containing monochromatic types.

Proof:
1. subtract `∑ τ c τ · (fixed copy of type τ)` to kill the edge-count vector;
2. at every non-base vertex `v`, subtract the difference gadgets
   `T(v,x,y) - T(o,x,y)` (`exists_deg_gadget`), which move the degree vector of `v` to the base
   vertex `o` of its class; the base vertex ends with the class sum, which is the (zero)
   edge-count vector;
3. the residual is balanced, hence physical (`physDivZ_of_zeroDeg`).
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace PartitionedTriangleAbsorption.BlowupB

open Finset

